               "body" : {
                  "content" : [
                     {
                        "content" : [
                           {
                              "text" : "MAYBE instead of ptr to T, add extra level of indirection T**, or better unique_ptr<T>* instead of T*? - so deserializer can allocate the object? Cost overhead? but still allow subclassing.",
                              "type" : "text"
                           }
                        ],
                        "type" : "paragraph"
                     },
                     {
                        "type" : "paragraph"
                     },
                     {
                        "content" : [
                           {
                              "text" : "But not really that simple. Issue is - ToObject code currently just fills in fields and assumes object passed in OK/constructed.",
                              "type" : "text"
                           }
                        ],
                        "type" : "paragraph"
                     },
                     {
                        "content" : [
                           {
                              "text" : "If we add extra indrection (or somehow - like with optional - havent constructed - must construct in first class we run into the call).",
                              "type" : "text"
                           }
                        ],
                        "type" : "paragraph"
                     },
                     {
                        "content" : [
                           {
                              "text" : "But in current system, this is BASE class - not most specific class.",
                              "type" : "text"
                           }
                        ],
                        "type" : "paragraph"
                     }
